From 6abefa5177eddd4ae28e7b9bbe7abea4bd8dd089 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leon Seemann <leon@seemann.nrw>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:18:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] zink: update the pipeline when only the vertex input state
 changes

Without VK_EXT_vertex_input_dynamic_state the vertex input state is baked
into the pipeline. Binding new vertex elements only sets
ctx->vertex_state_changed, which zink_get_gfx_pipeline() uses to rehash
the vertex state, but zink_draw() does not check it before calling
update_gfx_pipeline() and clears it after the draw. A draw that only
changes the vertex layout (same program, otherwise unchanged state) then
keeps using the previous pipeline with the wrong attribute formats and
offsets.

Seen on KosmicKrisp, which lacks vertex input dynamic state: two draws
with the same program but different vertex layouts (display list replay
vs. a regular VAO) break each other, whichever comes first in a batch
wins. Also reproducible on lavapipe with the extension disabled.

Cc: mesa-stable
Closes: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/issues/16562
Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/45132>
---
 src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_draw.cpp | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_draw.cpp b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_draw.cpp
index 52d5c96d48ee..d3539e0c1f29 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_draw.cpp
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_draw.cpp
@@ -749,8 +749,12 @@ zink_draw(struct pipe_context *pctx,
    if (have_streamout && ctx->dirty_so_targets)
       zink_emit_stream_output_targets(pctx);
 
+   /* without dynamic vertex input, the vertex input state is part of the pipeline */
+   const bool vertex_input_changed = DYNAMIC_STATE != ZINK_DYNAMIC_VERTEX_INPUT &&
+                                     DYNAMIC_STATE != ZINK_DYNAMIC_VERTEX_INPUT2 &&
+                                     ctx->vertex_state_changed;
    bool pipeline_changed = false;
-   if (ctx->gfx_pipeline_state.dirty || rp_state != ctx->gfx_pipeline_state.rp_state || ctx->gfx_dirty || ctx->dirty_gfx_stages || prim_changed || BATCH_CHANGED) {
+   if (ctx->gfx_pipeline_state.dirty || rp_state != ctx->gfx_pipeline_state.rp_state || ctx->gfx_dirty || ctx->dirty_gfx_stages || prim_changed || vertex_input_changed || BATCH_CHANGED) {
       if (!update_gfx_pipeline<DYNAMIC_STATE, BATCH_CHANGED>(ctx, bs, mode, &pipeline_changed))
          return;
    }
